          "type": "info_box",
          "title": "Key Concepts: Idioms & Emphatic Stress",
          "prompt": "",
          "text": "1. **Idioms & Collocations:** Figurative expressions like 'sinking feeling' (a sudden feeling of dread) or 'haul over the coals' (to scold severely) must be understood in context.\n2. **Emphatic Syllable Stress:** When using adverbs of emphasis (e.g., *rapidly*, *completely*), we place extra stress on one specific syllable. Your voice rises slightly on this syllable to draw focus and add strength to the sentence."
